// Trade messages (Plan/11 section 4.2, WP-PROTO-16; tag block 384-415): the player-to-player trade handshake,
// the personal vendor (private shop) and the vendor chat rooms. Transcribed from ref/07b sections 10, 19 and
// 20, ref/07c section 5, ref/08 sections 12.3-12.4, ref/09a section 5.x, ref/09b section 3.9, ref/13 sections
// 14-15 and Plan/19 sections 8 and 9.
//
// Trade state machine (Plan/19 section 8): ConfirmTradeReq (request) -> ConfirmTradeNtf to the target; TradeReq
// (accept) -> TradeNtf to both; TradePutReq / TradePullReq / TradePutGoldReq edit the offers (echoed to both);
// TradeOkReq -> TradeOkNtf, and when both are OK TradeLastConfirm; TradeConfirm -> TradeLastConfirmOk, and when
// both confirmed the commit and TradeConsent. TradeCancelReq / errors -> TradeCancelNtf to both. Every item
// travels as its inventory OBJECT ID; the offers stay in the owner's inventory as reservations until the
// commit.
//
// FIX shapes (Plan/11a, PL-062, PL-063, VR-017; ledger draft in the NOTES of this crate): TradeNtf does NOT
// carry the partner's inventory (the legacy sent the whole CItemContainer of the other player); TradePutNtf
// carries the offered ItemElem instead, so the browser needs no partner inventory copy; the gold of
// TradePutGoldReq accumulates and TradePutGoldNtf carries the running total; a ConfirmTradeReq creates a
// pending request that TradeReq must match.
//
// Vendor: RegisterPVendorItemReq (while closed) -> PVendorOpenReq (title) -> buyers QueryPVendorItem /
// BuyPVendorItem -> PVendorCloseReq. The chat room of a shop is keyed by the vendor's player id (ChattingNtf
// sub-types).

